{{!--
  page.navigation is Antora's own array of root menus — one per unordered
  list per nav file listed in the component descriptor's `nav` key, in that
  same order. A component with a single nav file therefore has exactly one,
  `{ root: true, items: [...] }`, carrying neither `content` nor `url`;
  nav-tree.hbs treats an item with neither as a transparent wrapper (see its
  own comment) so real top-level entries land at level 0, not level 1.

  A component with SEVERAL nav files has one root menu per module, and this
  renders only the one the current page belongs to — the side menu shows a
  single module at a time, with nav-switcher.hbs moving between them. That
  is the same shape Fumadocs had, where each module's meta.json declared
  `"root": true` and the sidebar rendered only the innermost root folder on
  the current path.

  `module` is not Antora's: it is stamped onto each tree by
  @inditextech/pdocs-antora-extensions from the descriptor's `nav_modules`
  key. When it is absent — no extension, or a site that never declared any —
  every tree renders, which is exactly what a single-nav-file site did
  before any of this existed.
--}}
{{#each page.navigation}}
{{#if (or (not ./module) (eq ./module @root.page.module))}}
{{> nav-tree navigation=./items level=0}}
{{/if}}
{{/each}}
